\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Our Lord is risen from the dead!
\par Our Jesus is gone up on high!
\par The powers of hell are captive led,
\par Dragged to the portals of the sky.
\par                                         Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There His triumphal chariot waits,
\par And angels chant the solemn lay:
\par Lift up your heads, ye heavenly gates;
\par Ye everlasting doors, give way;
\par                                           Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Loose all your bars of massy light,
\par And wide unfold the etheral scene:
\par He claims these mansions as His right;
\par Receive the King of Glory in!
\par                                             Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Who is this King of Glory? Who?
\par The Lord that all our foes o'er came,
\par The world sin, death, and hell o'erthrew;
\par And Jesus is the Conqueror's name.
\par                                                 Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lo! His triumphal chariot waits,
\par And angels chant the solemn lay;
\par Lift up your heads, ye heavenly gates;
\par Ye everlasting doors, give way;
\par                                           Hallelujah.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Who is this King of Glory? Who?
\par The Lord, of glorious power possest;
\par The King of saints, and angels too,
\par God over all, for ever blest!
\par                                    Hallelujah.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

